      "seq": 24,
      "kind": "submit",
      "at": 1791588961767,
      "reason": "In BasicTokenizer.train and RegexTokenizer.train, the per-merge argmax `max(stats, key=stats_get)` called dict.get and re-hashed a tuple for every pair. It is replaced by C-level max/count/index over list(stats.values()). When there is a single maximum, the pair is taken with islice at that index, which is the same first-maximal key that max() returns. Ties go through the existing first-occurrence scan unchanged. Outputs are identical (equivalence harness passes, tests pass); train_ir ratio is 0.926."
    }
